  "problem": "Which of the following vector spaces has a dimension of $36?$\n\n- ${R}_{6}[t]$, the vector space of all polynomials in the variable $t$ of degree at most $6$\n- ${\\text{M}}_{12\\times 3}(R),$ the vector space of all $12\\times 3$ matrices over $R$\n- ${R}^{36}$",
  "worked_solution": "Let's examine each of the vector spaces in turn.\n\n- Recall that $\\text{dim}({R}_{n}[t])=n+1.$ Therefore, \n\n$$\n\\text{dim}({R}_{6}[t])=6+1=7\\ne 36.\\,\\times \n$$\n- Recall that $\\text{dim}({\\text{M}}_{n\\times m}(R))=n\\cdot m.$ Therefore, \n\n$$\n\\text{dim}({\\text{M}}_{12\\times 3}(R))=12\\cdot 3=36.\\,\u2713\n$$\n- Recall that $\\text{dim}({R}^{n})=n.$ Therefore, \n\n$$\n\\text{dim}({R}^{36})=36.\\,\u2713\n$$\n\nHence, the correct answer is \"II and III only.\"",
